  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-09-19T02:39:55.709Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Inspired from this thread: https://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/auto-safety-mode\nI'd like to suggest a new pre-set option for the Safety menu -- as an instance's population increases, Safety settings can be enabled for non-friends, and heightened automatically as the instance fills up.\nI feel like the dynamic rubber-banding of these Safety can help improve quality of life to performance-heavy worlds, such as those that utilize stream players and real-time audio-based shaders. It seems common to go to a big event and spend minutes at a time sorting out your menu while experiencing frame drops, even though Panic mode isn't necessary to enable.\nExample:\n20 users - Shaders/particles/anims hidden for anyone below User rank\n30 users - Avatars hidden/fallbacked for Known user and below\n40+ users - Non-friends hidden/fallbacked; voice off for Visitor rank",
